Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:16:41 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] frontend: homework follows the server's personal copies
 and atomic split

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011d4mgSxngjRmAXosGe4ry4

- Submitting a shared group task returns the student's own copy (new id); the
  list now replaces the row that was submitted.
- 'Split per student' is one server call instead of N creates + a delete that
  could half-fail.
- Homework list shows a load error with retry instead of a toast and an empty list.
- Relative times come from a ticking clock (useNow).
